  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n1/(x+3) + 1/(x+5) = 1/6\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nQuadratic formula: x = (-b ± √(b² - 4ac)) / (2a)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ (x+5 + x+3) / ((x+3)(x+5)) = 1/6\n\n⇒ (2x + 8) / (x² + 8x + 15) = 1/6\n\n⇒ 6(2x + 8) = x² + 8x + 15\n\n⇒ 12x + 48 = x² + 8x + 15\n\n⇒ x² - 4x - 33 = 0\n\nCoefficients: a=1, b=-4, c=-33\n\n⇒ x = (-(-4) ± √((-4)² - 4 × 1 ×(-33))) / (2 × 1)\n\n⇒ x = (4 ± √(16 + 132)) / 2\n\n⇒ x = (4 ± √(148)) / 2\n\n⇒ x = x = 2 ± √37\n\n**∴ Option 4 is the correct answer.**",
